# Source is text, even when a stray byte says otherwise.
#
# src/servers.ts spent some time committed with two NUL bytes inside it, which
# put it over git's binary heuristic: `git diff` and every review surface said
# "Binary file differs" and showed nothing. A file you cannot read the diff of
# is a file that gets changed without review, which is the actual cost.
#
# `diff` forces a textual diff regardless of the heuristic; `text` normalises
# line endings on the way in. Neither changes what is stored.
*.ts  text diff
*.tsx text diff
*.rs  text diff
*.css text diff
